Found it: `clamp()` returns the upper bound when its bounds are inverted, and `scroll.ts` calls it that way. Here is the change and how I would land it:

```a2ui
surface("review")
$/scope = ["patch"]
$/regression = true
$/note = "fix(math): clamp() handles negative input"
diff = Diff("""@@ -12,7 +12,10 @@ export function clamp(value: number, min: number, max: number) {
-  return Math.min(Math.max(value, min), max);
+  if (min > max) {
+    throw new RangeError(`clamp: min ${min} > max ${max}`);
+  }
+  return Math.min(Math.max(value, min), max);
 }""", path="src/math.ts")
checks = Activity([{icon: "terminal", label: "vp test run src/math.test.ts", detail: "12 passed"}, {icon: "search", label: "Searched callers of clamp()", detail: "7 files"}, {icon: "circle-alert", label: "src/scroll.ts passes min > max", detail: "line 88", failed: true}])
scope = Choice([{label: "Patch only", value: "patch"}, {label: "Patch + fix scroll.ts", value: "both"}, {label: "Open a PR", value: "pr"}], $/scope, label="How should I land it?")
regression = Switch("Add a regression test", $/regression, description="Covers min > max in math.test.ts")
note = Field("Commit message", $/note)
apply = Button("Apply", Event("apply", {scope: $/scope, regression: $/regression, note: $/note}), tone="primary")
skip = Button("Not now", Event("skip"), tone="ghost")
root = Panel([diff, checks, scope, regression, note, Stack([apply, skip], direction="horizontal", gap="small")], title="clamp() rejects inverted bounds", description="One change in src/math.ts. scroll.ts calls it the wrong way round.")
```
